{"success":true,"data":{"id":"battletech-simulator-arxdo2-mrz2ryvkgzv","title":"Combat Modifiers Fix - Target movement, min range, partial cover","description":"Combat Modifiers Fix - Target movement, min range, partial cover.\n\nFIXES NEEDED:\n1. Target movement modifier - Implement based on hexes moved:\n   - 0 hexes: +0\n   - 1-2 hexes: +1\n   - 3-4 hexes: +2\n   - 5-6 hexes: +3\n   - 7-9 hexes: +4\n   - 10+ hexes: +5\n   Track hexesMoved on unit during movement phase.\n\n2. Minimum range formula - Fix off-by-one. Current: minRange - distance + 1. Correct: minRange - distance. PPC at range 2 should be +1, not +2.\n\n3. Partial cover direction - Currently subtracts -1 (easier). Should add +1 (harder) AND switch to punch hit location table.\n\n4. Targeting Computer - Expand to include DB weapons (AC/2, AC/5, AC/10, AC/20, Machine Gun) and P-type weapons, not just DE.\n\n5. Prone attack modifier - Adjacent attacker vs prone target = -2, non-adjacent = -4. Code always uses -4.\n\n6. Woods blocking logic - LOS blocks at density  Should block at 3+ HEXES of woods, not density. 1 heavy + 1 light = 2 hexes, should NOT block.\n\nTEST: Write tests for each modifier. Verify GATOR calculations match BMM examples.","status":"open","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2026-07-24T15:08:33.488Z","updated_at":"2026-07-24T15:08:55.091Z","parent_id":"battletech-simulator-arxdo2-mrz2ryu6vqj","dependencies":[],"metadata":{}}}
